    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look for offensive production today led by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), who represent our clearest paths to category gains. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Young (xERA 4.78) and a park environment that adds 16% to his base projection, while **Gunnar Henderson**\u2019s elite power profile is bolstered by a massive 16% park adjustment against Yesavage. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also presents a high-floor start at 70.88, as his dynamic platoon advantage against King provides a reliable anchor for our middle infield.\n\nWe navigated a congested outfield, with **Miguel Andujar** (59.13) edging out several candidates due to a 12% boost from a favorable platoon matchup against Griffin. The most difficult bench decision involved **Coby Mayo** (49.79), who narrowly missed the cut despite a strong park factor. Ultimately, **Coby Mayo** was relegated to the bench because his dynamic platoon split against Yesavage was insufficient to overcome the higher raw efficiency of the starting utility and outfield group. **Nasim Nunez** remains in the lineup despite a low order spot, as we prioritize his speed potential in a categories-constrained environment, even against a tough hold from King.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the three \"Lineup Pending\" statuses for **Dominic Smith**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Andy Pages**. While **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** are projected for sub-50 scores due to the elite skill profile of Luzardo (xERA 3.28), any shift into the top-third of the order would necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily cap usage. Managers should specifically monitor the catch-and-throw metrics against **Andy Pages**, as his 62% SB-hold risk against him further complicates his appeal today if he fails to secure a premium batting position.",
